qrabackup (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * restic Test connection button with plain-language failure diagnosis
    (wrong password, bad S3 keys, missing repo, stale lock, unreachable
    endpoint) — hints also shown on every restic error.
  * restic Unlock button (remove stale repository locks).
  * Export… button: save repository URL, password and S3 keys to a
    plaintext 0600 file as an offline recovery escrow.
  * Snapshots/Stats/Forget dry-run no longer block the UI; Stop cancels.
  * Per-profile last-run status (ok/fail, time, duration) in the profile
    list, persisted across restarts.
  * Fix: deleting a profile no longer overwrites the next profile with
    the deleted one's settings.
  * Fix: a corrupt settings.json is backed up (.corrupt.bak) instead of
    being silently overwritten on the next save.
  * Fix: settings tmp file is created with 0600 permissions from the
    first byte (secrets were briefly world-readable during saves).
  * Fix: startup no longer crashes on a corrupted window-geometry blob.

 -- Vlad Ananyev <vlananyev@gmail.com>  Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

qrabackup (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * restic/S3 engine: encrypted, deduplicated backups to S3-compatible
    stores, with init/snapshots/restore/check/forget+prune/stats.
  * Unified run-step queue; retention (forget --prune) after backup.
  * Refactor into qrabackup_app package; unit test suite.

